{"en":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":""},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\"></span> The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/ability\" title=\"ability\">ability</a> of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/brain\" title=\"brain\">brain</a> to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/record\" title=\"record\">record</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/information\" title=\"information\">information</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/impression\" title=\"impression\">impressions</a> with the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/facility\" title=\"facility\">facility</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/recalling\" title=\"recalling\">recalling</a> them later, usually <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/at_will\" title=\"at will\">at will</a>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<b>Memory</b> is a facility common to all animals."}],"examples":["<b>Memory</b> is a facility common to all animals."]},{"definition":"A record of a thing or an event stored and available for later use by an organism.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"I have no <b>memory</b> of that event."},{"example":"My wedding is one of my happiest <b>memories</b>."},{"example":"Sam and his friends will never forget the happy <b>memories</b> of the field trip to France."}],"examples":["I have no <b>memory</b> of that event.","My wedding is one of my happiest <b>memories</b>.","Sam and his friends will never forget the happy <b>memories</b> of the field trip to France."]},{"definition":""},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\"></span> The part of a computer that stores variable executable code or data (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/RAM\" title=\"RAM\">RAM</a>) or unalterable executable code or default data (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/ROM\" title=\"ROM\">ROM</a>).","parsedExamples":[{"example":"This data passes from the CPU to the <b>memory</b>."}],"examples":["This data passes from the CPU to the <b>memory</b>."]},{"definition":"The time within which past events can be or are remembered.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"in recent <b>memory</b>"},{"example":"in living <b>memory</b>"}],"examples":["in recent <b>memory</b>","in living <b>memory</b>"]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt47\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> Of a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/material\" title=\"material\">material</a>, which <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/return\" title=\"return\">returns</a> to its <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/original\" title=\"original\">original</a> <span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\" about=\"#mwt48\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/shape#English\" title=\"shape\">shape</a></span> when <span class=\"Latn\" lang=\"en\" about=\"#mwt49\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/heat#English\" title=\"heat\">heated</a></span>.","parsedExamples":[{"example":"<b>memory</b> metal"},{"example":"<b>memory</b> plastic"}],"examples":["<b>memory</b> metal","<b>memory</b> plastic"]},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt52\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/memorial\" title=\"memorial\">memorial</a>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt54\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt55\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">Synonym of <span class=\"form-of-definition-link\"><i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/pelmanism#English\" title=\"pelmanism\">pelmanism</a></i> <span class=\"mention-gloss-paren annotation-paren\">(</span><span class=\"mention-gloss-double-quote\">“</span><span class=\"mention-gloss\">memory card game</span><span class=\"mention-gloss-double-quote\">”</span><span class=\"mention-gloss-paren annotation-paren\">)</span></span></span>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt58\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <span class=\"maintenance-line\" about=\"#mwt59\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">(<span id=\"rfv-sense-notice-en-\"></span>Can we <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Wiktionary:Requests_for_verification/English#memory\" title=\"Wiktionary:Requests for verification/English\">verify</a> this sense?)</span><link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:Requests_for_verification_in_English_entries#MEMORY\" about=\"#mwt59\"> <span class=\"use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt60\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/term_of_venery#English\" title=\"term of venery\">term of venery</a> for a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/social#English\" title=\"social\">social</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/group#English\" title=\"group\">group</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/elephants#English\" title=\"elephants\">elephants</a>, normally called a <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/herd#English\" title=\"herd\">herd</a></i>.</span>"}]}],"nl":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"Dutch","definitions":[{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/pelmanism\" title=\"pelmanism\">pelmanism</a>; a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/memory#English\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\">memory</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/card_game\" title=\"card game\">card game</a> in which a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/pack\" title=\"pack\">pack</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/card\" title=\"card\">cards</a> is spread out <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/face-down\" title=\"face-down\">face-down</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/player\" title=\"player\">players</a> try to turn up <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/pair\" title=\"pair\">pairs</a> with the same <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/symbol\" title=\"symbol\">symbol</a>."}]}]}